cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the repository version and the associated manuscript for the component you use. If you use Original FDPL or the earlier dual-branch study, also cite the CMC 2026 paper listed in README.md."
title: "Residual FDPL and Risk-Controlled RGB Correction"
abstract: "Reference software for two related studies in real-world image denoising: Residual Frequency Domain Perception Loss and risk-controlled residual RGB correction after a denoiser has been frozen. The RGB-correction component includes exact zero-luma and pre-clipping error identities, paired endpoint calibration, frozen protocols, and compact aggregate results. The accompanying manuscripts are 'Residual Frequency Domain Perception Loss for Real-World Image Denoising with Adaptive Spectral Supervision' and 'Residual Color Correction after Real-World Image Denoising: Transfer Boundaries and Risk-Controlled Endpoint Calibration'. The earlier Original FDPL method is described in the CMC 2026 paper 'A Lightweight Dual-Branch CNN with Frequency Domain Perception Loss for Image Denoising'."
